                        "email": "moiseev.ivan4w@yandex.com",
                        "username": "rainar4w"
                    },
                    "message": "How could it affect user lock out?\nThis change reports correct user enabled state if user account has expired.\nWhile user lock out settings are responsible for locking a user after given number of failed login attempts, which is not the same as user account expiration.\nI've checked that `test_user_manager` test runs without fails.\nDo you have other tests/scenarios in mind which might be worth checking?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "user_mgr.cpp",
                    "line": 1003,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ravi Teja",
                        "email": "raviteja28031990@gmail.com",
                        "username": "raviteja-b"
                    },
                    "message": "this code hit in user locked out case, so asked if you have verified account lockout"
                },
                {
                    "file": "user_mgr.cpp",
                    "line": 1003,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ivan Moiseev",
                        "email": "moiseev.ivan4w@yandex.com",
                        "username": "rainar4w"
                    },
                    "message": "This commentary is incorrect. As function name implies code checks for user enabled/disabled state which is different from user lock out. That is why I removed this misleading comment."
                },
                {
                    "file": "user_mgr.cpp",
                    "line": 1003,
                    "reviewer": {
